[_] Provision image-owned agents, rootless Podman and private shpool workspace tooling =mini-server-agent-tools $Owner requested frequent agent use and clarifies existing sandboxes run agents as root inside each sandbox; no dedicated/per-agent host user. Reuse existing sandbox launcher and validate concurrent sandbox isolation, scoped state/credentials, host versus sandbox tool composition and shpool compatibility with namespace helpers. Exact core pins and integrity-locked build prototype staged; 93 offline tests pass, no actual Fedora build or agent/session/SELinux VM pass. Pin executable extensions, retain runtime-only authentication, review shpool linger/reconnect/reboot state recovery before activation. Owner explicitly requests core Podman/rootless host integration: explicit podman/container-selinux/crun/netavark/passt/fuse-overlayfs/shadow-utils-subid RPMs; enrolled account receives recorded stable non-overlapping subuid/subgid blocks with partial-write retries and no remapping of mutable state. Enable operator linger once, preserving later explicit disable. shpool now sets NoNewPrivileges=no for mapping helpers/operator sudo, not as a sandbox; shpool/API sockets/auto-update/restart remain disabled. Original account-journal schema retained with separate rootless ledger; native checks fixed invalid CREATE_MAIL_SPOOL -K and NSS authselect/factory links. 119 offline tests plus native Fedora useradd/getsubids/Shadow-lock bridge pass (logind mocked, protected synthetic state). Latest integration unbuilt; rootless/shpool/linger/cgroup/SELinux boot and update/rollback still required. No live account/services/credentials/submodule/platform changes; sandbox extraction delegated to another agent. Latest owner direction supersedes mandatory root-inside-sandbox use for the independent disposable dev pod: agents may run as pod root, with sandboxes only when useful, no operational/personal state and provider auth/private keys kept on the controller. Dev no longer depends on services enrollment/rootless-user/chezmoi/shpool readiness. Arch dev profile source now exists; next build/boot root access and perform one useful task with only needed tools. Retained Fedora payload and existing sandbox extraction remain separate; do not restart integration/recovery machinery by default.$ !2 ^2026-10-03T00:47 %2026-10-19T04:39 #01a100bb-1257-7773-a8d0-e0132fa370b0
